# Static Site → Next.js Migration

Reference: `uis/website_v1/SPEC.md`, `memory-bank/rules/`.

## Parity requirements

Ship all five views with shared navbar/footer: Home, Catalog, Product, Cart, Checkout (3 steps).

Preserve SEO from the reference (semantic HTML, meta tags, JSON-LD where present). Verify responsive layout at ~375px, ~768px, ~1280px.

## Component extraction

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — reusable, typed, shared chrome
import type { Product } from '@repo/shared-types';

export function ProductCard({ product }: { product: Product }) { ... }

// ❌ BAD — inline duplicate schema
interface Product { id: string; name: string; ... }
```

Extract: Navbar, Footer, ProductCard, CartLineItem, CheckoutSteps. Match design tokens from `website_v1` Tailwind config.

## Data & backend

- Use mock/placeholder product data until backend milestone.
- Cart and checkout stay client-side or mocked — no payment API integration without explicit request.
- When adding types, extend `packages/shared/types/index.ts`, not local duplicates.

## Visual fidelity

Carry forward colors (`navbase`, `oat`, `clay`, etc.), typography (Manrope/Spectral), and spacing. Do not redesign unless asked.
